From 44f3ca1e39d1ca87ad816bbe22499b07569a976b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 16:01:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): release legacy goal completions, long receipts
 and archives at the origin [daveey]

- Goal cards completed before the board's first goal_verified receipt are owner-verified on basis
  legacy_completed (closing run + local-only contract; completed event bound to that run when the board
  still has it). Receipt-era cards without a receipt stay unverified; boards with no receipt get no pass.
- Receipt evidence is compared with the closing run's full handoff when the completed event only kept its
  first line (400 chars): 13 of 15 hub receipts could never verify before.
- An owner-observed archive without a verified completion closes the origin obligation as
  closed_uncompleted (not unfinished, never released/completed), in the ledger and the replica link reader.
